--- a/packages/web/src/content/docs/tui.mdx
+++ b/packages/web/src/content/docs/tui.mdx
@@ -375,6 +375,11 @@ You can customize TUI behavior through `tui.json` (or `tui.jsonc`).
     "style": "block",
     "blinking": true
   },
+  "terminal": {
+    "title": {
+      "prefix": "OC | "
+    }
+  },
   "mouse": true,
   "attention": {
     "enabled": true,
@@ -403,6 +408,7 @@ This is separate from `opencode.json`, which configures server/runtime behavior.
 - `diff_style` - Controls diff rendering. `"auto"` adapts to terminal width, `"stacked"` always shows a single-column layout.
 - `cursor` - Controls the terminal cursor in TUI input fields. `style` defaults to `"block"`, can be `"underline"`, `"line"`, or `"default"`; `blinking` defaults to `true`. When `style` is `"default"`, the terminal default cursor is restored, so `blinking` has no effect.
 - `mouse` - Enable or disable mouse capture in the TUI (default: `true`). When disabled, the terminal's native mouse selection/scrolling behavior is preserved.
+- `terminal.title.prefix` - Prefix shown before the session title in the terminal window/tab title. Defaults to `"OC | "`. Set to `""` to remove the prefix.
 - `sidebar.width` - Controls the width of the session sidebar in terminal columns. Defaults to `42`.
 - `sidebar.position` - Controls which side of the terminal the session sidebar renders on. Can be `"left"` or `"right"`. Defaults to `"right"`.
 - `attention` - Configures TUI desktop notifications and sounds. Disabled by default.
